 location="Dorsal closed medulla just above the pyramidal decussation, medial (gracile) and lateral (cuneate) to each other under the tubercles that bulge into the caudal floor of the fourth ventricle region; the accessory cuneate nucleus lies lateral to the cuneate nucleus.",
 function="Second-order relay of discriminative touch, vibration and conscious proprioception; the site of the somatotopic hand-over from ipsilateral to contralateral representation.",
